From 95aea95f2735094de287d88e3e5edd063a415463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 16:02:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] audio.service: set NDK binder threadpool max before
 starting the pool
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the fydroid ARC container the vendor libbinder_ndk shares the single vendor
libbinder ProcessState (driver /dev/vndbinder) with ::android::ProcessState in
the audio HAL service — they are not split across /dev/binder and /dev/vndbinder
as on a stock VNDK device. So the stock main() order —
ProcessState::self()->startThreadPool() (starts the pool at the default max of
15) followed by ABinderProcess_setThreadPoolMaxThreadCount(1) — aborts the
process with "Binder threadpool cannot be shrunk after starting".

That killed android.hardware.audio.service on every start, so audioserver never
published media.audio_policy; system_server then blocked in
AudioProductStrategy.native_list_audio_product_strategies() during AudioService
startup until the Watchdog killed system_server (boot loop).

Move ABinderProcess_setThreadPoolMaxThreadCount(1) before startThreadPool() so
the max is set while the pool is unstarted. No-op on stock (the two ProcessState
instances are distinct there); fixes the abort in the container.

Verified on device: audio-hal + audioserver stay up, StartAudioService
completes in 16ms, system_server advances past AudioService through late boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I9a2da3ba80a3892ed9cf4970148dcc91b4cc2007
---
 .../all-versions/default/service/service.cpp     | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/audio/common/all-versions/default/service/service.cpp b/audio/common/all-versions/default/service/service.cpp
index fbf616563d..9959687094 100644
--- a/audio/common/all-versions/default/service/service.cpp
+++ b/audio/common/all-versions/default/service/service.cpp
@@ -76,10 +76,22 @@ int main(int /* argc */, char* /* argv */ []) {
     signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN);
 
     ::android::ProcessState::initWithDriver("/dev/vndbinder");
-    // start a threadpool for vndbinder interactions
-    ::android::ProcessState::self()->startThreadPool();
 
+    // fydroid: set the NDK binder threadpool max BEFORE starting any pool.
+    // In the ARC container the vendor libbinder_ndk shares the single vendor
+    // libbinder ProcessState (driver /dev/vndbinder) with
+    // ::android::ProcessState::self() below — they are not split across
+    // /dev/binder and /dev/vndbinder as on a stock VNDK device. So calling
+    // ABinderProcess_setThreadPoolMaxThreadCount(1) AFTER startThreadPool()
+    // (which starts the pool at the default max of 15) aborts the process with
+    // "Binder threadpool cannot be shrunk after starting", killing the audio
+    // HAL -> audioserver never publishes media.audio_policy -> AudioService
+    // hangs -> Watchdog kills system_server. Setting the max first is a no-op on
+    // stock (separate ProcessStates) and avoids the shrink here.
     ABinderProcess_setThreadPoolMaxThreadCount(1);
+
+    // start a threadpool for vndbinder interactions
+    ::android::ProcessState::self()->startThreadPool();
     ABinderProcess_startThreadPool();
 
     const int32_t defaultValue = -1;
-- 
